# Translation of Odoo Server.
# This file contains Spanish (Argentina) translations for the Finance-facing
# vendor-bill LLM/OCR import flow.
#
# IMPORTANT (verified against odoo/tools/translate.py - CodeTranslations):
# a .po file placed outside its own module only works for model/model_terms
# entries (menu names, view labels, button strings, field labels) - Odoo
# resolves those generically by (model, xmlid, field) regardless of which
# module's i18n/ shipped the translation. Python _()-string translations
# ("code" type - chatter/banner messages, raised errors) are NOT: Odoo looks
# them up strictly from the i18n/ folder of the module whose source file
# contains the _() call (see CodeTranslations._get_po_paths). So this file
# can translate OCA/Apexive's own menu/view/button strings (they're
# model/model_terms), but NOT their own Python-raised messages - those stay
# English unless a .po is added inside those modules' own i18n/ directories,
# which this project has decided not to do (keeps third-party modules
# pristine). Only llm_invoice_ocr's own _()-wrapped messages below are
# translated here, since this IS their owning module.
#
